QuestGuidance.Register("en",218,{
[6945]="70047CD4\n1\tHas someone fallen into danger in Haudh Nogbenn?\t\n2\tYou have encountered a daring hobbit lass while searching for a way to cleanse the corruption from the sceptre that came out of Mordor.\t\n3\tExamine the tomb in Haudh Nogbenn\tThere is a tomb in Haudh Nogbenn. Is this the final resting place of the sceptre's owner?\n4\tListen to the words of the slain prince\tYour head is pounding.\n5\tMarigold Boffin is in Haudh Nogbenn.\t\n",
[6946]="70047CD8\n1\tTalk to Greith in the central chamber\tGreith is in the central chamber, by the tremendous geode.\n2\tSearch the northern chamber\tGreith has asked you to search the room to the north of the Chamber of Machurful.\n3\tTalk to Greith in the central chamber, just north of the geode\tGreith is in the central chamber, just north of the geode.\n4\tSearch the rooms to the east\tGreith has asked you to search the room to the east of the Chamber of Machurful.\n5\tTalk to Greith in the central chamber, just east of the geode\tGreith is in the central chamber, just east of the geode.\n6\tSearch the southern chamber and return to Greith\tGreith has asked you to search the room to the south of the Chamber of Machurful.\n7\tDefeat Grotcleaver\tGrotcleaver, a tremendous deep-claw, has made its home in the Chamber of Machurful. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n8\tTalk to Greith\tGreith survived the battle with Grotcleaver, and wishes to speak with you.\n",
[6947]="70066951\n1\tTalk to Nathlad by the bridges that cross the River Anduin\tNathlad has brought you down to the bridges that now cross the Anduin, above which stands the city of Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Nathlad\tNathlad has ended his patrol and now stands before you, deep in thought.\n3\tListen to the words of Nathlad\tNathlad has ended his patrol and now stands before you, deep in thought.\n4\tTalk to Nathlad\tNathlad has come to a conclusion.\n",
[6948]="70047CD5\n1\tThere must be some way to get into the innermost chamber of the Lost Temple, where Elrond believes the corrupted cup might be redeemed.\t\n2\tTalk to Fithákh in the inner chamber\tFithákh, a cultist of the Corcur, has gained entrance to the innermost chamber of the Lost Temple. She seems to be expecting someone.\n3\tSet the corrupted cup on the central tomb\tFithákh asked you to set the cup on the tomb in the middle of the inner chamber, saying that it will serve as an altar for a sacrifice.\n4\tYou have done what you set out to do, and now you can either leave the chamber with haste or put an end to Fithákh's villainy.\t\n",
[6949]="70047CDC\n1\tTalk to Rattleleaf and hear his tale\tRattleleaf is by the still pool beneath Kar Lak, waiting to tell you his tale.\n2\tTalk to Rattleleaf and get him back on track\tRattleleaf seems to have distracted himself, and needs reminding of the story he was going to tell.\n3\tListen to Rattleleaf's tale\tRhothlas has begun to tell you the tale of what he saw by the still pool.\n4\tTalk to Rattleleaf\tRattleleaf has told you the story of Trotsiv, unhappy though it was.\n5\tTalk to Rattleleaf\tRattleleaf is by the pool beneath Kar Lak.\n",
[6950]="70047CD3\n1\tTalk to Walgar at the Spring of the Red-maid\tYou have come with some Eglain warriors to the Spring of the Red-maid. Here it may be that you can remove the corruption that encircles the carving of Darothild.\n2\tDefend Walgar from the Woman at the Spring\tYou have survived the onslaught of enemies at the Spring of the Red-maid, but now a mysterious figure has revealed herself.\n3\tTalk to Darothild's shade\tYou know beyond any doubt: this is the shade of Darothild, who fell at the Spring of the Red-maid.\n4\tEase Darothild's pain\tDarothild's shade stands before you at the Spring of the Red-maid, where she lost her final battle.\n5\tShow the corrupted sculpture to Darothild's shade\tDarothild's shade stands before you at the Spring of the Red-maid, where she lost her final battle. Walgar has asked you to show the corrupted sculpture to Darothild's shade.\n6\tTalk to Walgar at the Spring of the Red-maid\tWalgar is at the Spring of the Red-maid.\n",
[6951]="70047CD7\n1\tTalk to Techeron at the Bridge of Ariant\tThe Ranger Techeron is at the Bridge of Ariant, in Annúminas.\n2\tTalk to Techeron\tThe Ranger Techeron is near the Bridge of Ariant.\n",
[6952]="70058694\n1\tTalk to Umín\tUmín stands outside the docked ship, waiting to speak with you.\n2\tInvestigate the forsaken ship\tOthers have come to the lost ship for some unknown purpose, and you should learn what they intend.\n3\tDefeat Mal Stackwort's crew of cutthroats\tMal Stackwort, former minion of Bill Ferny, leads a crew of cutthroats intending to free the forsaken ship from its trapped berth.\n4\tTalk to Mal Stackwort\tMal Stackwort has no idea of the meaning behind Umín's words, and has asked you to explain them.\n5\tRemain on your guard\tUmín's words have had an effect on Mal Stackwort, but whether they will last remains to be seen.\n6\tTalk to Umín\tUmín has collected the necklace from where it lay, and he wishes to speak with you about it.\n",
[6953]="70047CDB\n1\tTalk to Tharbag\tTharbag's Orcs have captured Eldmath, and you really should free him... he was holding onto the corrupted tusk-shard when he was taken!\n2\tRemain alert and look for an opportunity to free Eldmath\tThe Orcs that captured Eldmath belong to the Boar-tribe and are led by Tharbag.\n3\tTalk to Skámash\tSkámash has been left in charge of dealing with you. This will likely prove to be a mistake!\n4\tSneak into Gris-shâtroful from the back\tGris-shâtroful is to the east, and you might be able to drop down from above and surprise the Orcs that captured Eldmath.\n5\tSurvive the encounter with Tharbag\tYou have found Eldmath, but the Orcs were alerted to your presence.\n6\tTalk to Eldmath\tEldmath is in Gris-shâtroful, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[6954]="70047CD6\n1\tTalk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä\tLothrandir is in the village of Sûri-kylä.\n2\tTalk to the Lossoth warrior in Sûri-kylä\tA Lossoth warrior has news of Pinja's whereabouts in Sûri-kylä.\n3\tFind Pinja and learn what has happened\tA Lossoth warrior claims that Pinja's dead husband Oiva has returned to life. How can this be?\n4\tTalk to Pinja in front of her home\tThe widow Pinja is outside her home, in Sûri-kylä.\n5\tExamine the unconscious body behind Pinja's home\tPinja told you that whatever has taken her husband Oiva's shape is currently unconscious behind her home.\n6\tRemain alert for any further treachery by Hamaito\tA spirit has masqueraded as Pinja's slain husband for its own cruel jest, but you have now revealed it.\n7\tDefeat Hamaito\tHamaito has revealed himself and seeks to avenge the spoiling of his jest. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n8\tTalk to Pinja\tHamaito has been defeated, and the corruption of Oiva's bone brooch has been cleansed.\n9\tTalk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä\tLothrandir is in Sûri-kylä.\n",
[6955]="70047CD9\n1\tTalk to Raiglud\tRaiglud, the oldest woman in Lhanuch, has begun to tell you a tale from her childhood.\n2\tListen to Raiglud's story\tRaiglud is telling you a tale from her childhood.\n3\tConsider Raiglud's description of Deilur\030Consider Raiglud's description of Maushkán\030Consider Raiglud's description of herself as a child\tRaiglud has told you she needs to rest a moment, for the telling of this tale is taking a lot out of her.\n4\tTalk to Raiglud and listen to the rest of her story\tRaiglud is ready to continue her tale.\n5\tListen to Raiglud's story\tRaiglud is telling you a tale from her childhood.\n6\tTalk to Raiglud\tRaiglud has told her story.\n",
[6956]="70047CDA\n1\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân inside the cave\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is inside the cave that was his brother's favourite place.\n2\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân inside the cave\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is inside the cave that was his brother's favourite place.\n3\tDescend to the lower chamber of the cave and confront the Orc\tAn Orc has found Bhai-buri-Ghân's cave.\n4\tConfront Turkalb\tThe Orc Turkalb has found Bhai-buri-Ghân's favourite cave.\n5\tHelp protect Khôr-buri-Ghân\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is in his brother's favourite cave.\n6\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân inside the cave\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is inside the cave that was his brother's favourite place.\n",
[6957]="700599F4\n1\tTalk to Durin in the court below the Steepset\tDurin stands with his personal guard Hrostyr not far from the Steepset, and he waits to speak with you.\n2\tClear the stairs leading to the Steepset of foes\tDurin asked you to clear the stairs leading to the Steepset of foes. Once you have accomplished this, he will rejoin you at the top of the stairs.\n3\tTalk to Durin atop the stairs near the Steepset\tNow that you have cleared the stairs of his foes, Durin can climb to the Steepset. He waits to speak with you at the top of the stairs.\n4\tHear the words of Durin before the Steepset\tDurin stands before the Steepset, the High Seat of the Lord of Gundabad.\n5\tTalk to Durin by the Steepset\tDurin stands by the Steepset, mourning for what has been lost.\n",
[6958]="700379DB\n1\tSpeak with Hildith\tHildith is in the Mead Hall of Grimslade.\n2\tListen to the council\tHildith's council is in the Mead Hall of Grimslade.\n3\tAsk Hildith why she was so harsh to Dunward\tHildith is in Grimslade's Mead Hall.\n4\tBow to Hildith and take your leave\tHildith is in Grimslade's Mead Hall.\n5\tWalk to the door\tYou should head towards the door of the Mead Hall.\n6\tLook back at Hildith from across the Mead Hall\tHildith is in the Grimslade Mead Hall.\n",
[6959]="7001C1C3\n1\tTalk to Fuirgam\tSpeak with Fuirgam and begin the assault upon the Orc fortress!\n2\tTalk to Fuirgam to end the battle and claim the fortress for the Malledhrim!\t\n",
[6960]="70053B2F\n1\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n2\tListen to Vágari's account\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n3\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n4\tListen to Vágari's account\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n5\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n6\tHear the words of Isildur as recounted by Vágari\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n7\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\t\n8\tListen to Vágari's account\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n9\tTalk to Gurnákh\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n10\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n",
[6961]="70030319\n1\tTalk to Corudan at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tCorudan's seat is just to your right, at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\n2\tListen to the conversation around the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tThe feast is over, but the conversation continues.\n3\tTalk to Ingyth at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tIngyth is at the table just to the right of her father, Ingbert, in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\n4\tTalk to Reeve Ingbert at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tReeve Ingbert is at the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\n5\tListen to the conversation around the table in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tThe feast is over, but the conversation continues.\n6\tTalk to Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\030Talk to Ingyth in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\030Talk to Nona in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tIngbert, Ingyth, and Nona have gotten up from the table and are each in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You should speak with each of them.\n7\tTalk to Horn inside the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tHorn is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\n8\tTalk to Horn outside the Mead Hall in Eaworth\tHorn is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\n9\tTalk to Horn outside the Mead Hall in Eaworth\tHorn is outside the Mead Hall, in Eaworth.\n",
[6962]="70028258\n1\tTalk to Mabon at Andras' homestead\tSpeak with Mabon at Andras' homestead.\n2\tDefeat the Dragon-clan raiders at Andras' homestead\tDefeat the Dragon-clan raiders at Andras' homestead.\n3\tTalk to Mabon at Andras' homestead\tSpeak with Mabon at Andras' homestead.\n4\tDefend Mabon at Andras' homestead\tDefend Mabon from the Dragon-clan raiders.\n5\tTalk to Mabon at Andras' homestead\tSpeak with Mabon at Andras' homestead.\n6\tDefend Andras' homestead\tDefend Andras' homestead from the Dragon-clan raiders.\n7\tTalk to the Dunlendings at Andras' farmstead\tSpeak with the Dunlendings at Andras' homestead.\n",
[6963]="700455DD\n1\tTalk to Burnoth\tBurnoth is standing on the field near Kings' End. You have arrived at the last location where Fastred sighted Crúmgam, and should now talk to Burnoth.\n2\tDefeat the ambushing foes\tThe ambushing foes can be found just ahead. You have begun your search for Crúmgam, but foes now harry your advance. You must defeat them!\n3\tSearch the charred fields for signs of Crúmgam\tFastred and the Riders Three are searching the fields outside Kings' End. You have survived an ambush and should now resume your search for Crúmgam.\n4\tDefeat the seeking flames\tCrúmgam's flames are upon one of the charred fields outside Kings' End. Vile flames have sprung to life and must now be quenched.\n5\tFollow Fastred as he seeks Crúmgam\tFastred is running through the charred fields outside Kings' End. You have witnessed Crúmgam's sorcery and should now search the nearby area for Crúmgam.\n6\tConfront Crúmgam\tCrúmgam is standing before the pyre outside Kings' End. You have found Crúmgam and beside him stands a man bearing the armour of the King's knights - a traitor deep within the heart of Rohan.\n7\tDefeat Brodwulf and avenge Léofdag\tBrodwulf is standing near the pyre outside Kings' End. Crúmgam has fled, leaving the traitor to his fate. You should defeat Brodwulf and avenge Léofdag.\n8\tTalk to Burnoth\tBurnoth is standing near the pyre outside Kings' End. You have defeated the traitor, Brodwulf, and should now speak to Burnoth.\n",
[6964]="70066BB2\n1\tTalk to your friend Valaric Túcca among the peaceful homes of the Holbytlan\tYour good friend Valaric Túcca can hardly believe that you have made the decision to leave.\n2\tMeet with Heldric Túcca as the sun rises\tMeet with Heldric Túcca outside his home in Lyndelby as the sun rises on the day you have decided to leave.\n3\tTalk to Grandmother Madelgard Túcca\tGrandmother Madelgard Túcca is waiting to speak with you as the sun rises on a beautiful day over the hidden Holbytlan village of Lyndelby.\n4\tTalk to Ogiva Túcca down the hill\030Talk to Vilihad on the path to the south\030Talk to Erma Túcca near the base of the hill\tGrandmother Maddy asked you to say good-bye to some of the early risers of Lyndelby.\n5\tTalk to Odger Túcca further along the path to the south-east\tYou have noticed Odger Túcca further down the path to the south-east, and should tell him about your plans.\n6\tWait for Croaker to reveal where he has gone\tOdger Túcca's best friend, his pet frog Croaker, has disappeared.\n7\tLook for Croaker near the rocks to the south-west\tOdger Túcca's best friend, his pet frog Croaker, has disappeared, but you heard his croaking near the rocks to the south-west.\n8\tProtect your friends and family from the goblins\tGoblins have snuck into the town of Lyndelby and now threaten your friends and family!\n9\tTalk to Fanglind, one of the Great Eagles who protects your people\tThe Eagle Fanglind has long protected the Holbytlan from any who find their hidden valley, and today has been no different.\n10\tSearch the goblin's satchel for a weapon to equip, and then talk to Fanglind\tFanglind has recommended that you search the satchel dropped by the goblins and equip one of the weapons you find within. Afterwards, he wants to talk to you some more.\n11\tTalk to Grandmother Maddy\tGrandmother Maddy stares at you with sadness, but with hope in her eyes as well.\n12\tWave to your friends and family, the good Holbytlan of Lyndelby, and begin your grand adventure\tGrandmother Maddy has asked you to wave to your friends and family, and then to begin your grand adventure.\n13\tYour journey demands that you help folk who need it\tYour adventure begins, and you vow to do as Grandmother Maddy requested: to help anyone who has need of it.\n14\tTalk to Meneldir and complete the quest 'A Larger World'\tThe man is strangely-dressed but seems friendly, and any foe of goblins or Orc-kind is a friend to the Holbytlan.\n",
[6965]="7006AFDE\n1\tTalk to Shaidal\tRothog has asked that you travel into the gladiator's residences and question Shaidal regarding the petition.\n2\tDefeat ambushers\tThe sounds of footsteps fill the halls, you are ambushed by attackers.\n3\tSpeak to Shaidal about the attack\tSpeak to Shaidal about the attack and what he will need of you.\n",
[6966]="70026E73\n1\tTalk to Ondor\tDefend Ondor as he works to collapse the cave-entrance.\n2\tOndor is at the Orc-cave. You should speak with Ondor the Dwarf once more.\t\n",
[6967]="70061CA4\n1\tDefeat the half-orcs on the road (total: 8)\tHalf-orcs harry travellers on the road through the Lone-lands. Candaith was right: the road to Rivendell is dangerous.\n2\tTalk to Galasebdir on the road through the Lone-lands\tGalasebdir, a Ranger of your acquaintance, has caught up to you on the road through the Lone-lands.\n3\tTalk to Galasebdir on the road through the Trollshaws\tYou have travelled with Galasebdir into the woods of the Trollshaws.\n4\tTalk to Galasebdir on the road through the Trollshaws\tYou have travelled with Galasebdir into the woods of the Trollshaws.\n5\tTalk to Galasebdir on the road through the High Moor\tYou have climbed up through the high moor with Galasebdir and are now near to the hidden vale of Rivendell.\n6\tTalk to Bregoleth\tAt the entrance to Rivendell, the Elf-warrior Bregoleth is pleased to see you.\n7\tFind the friend of whom Bregoleth spoke further along the path\tBregoleth told you a friend waits for you further along the path that descends into Rivendell.\n8\tTalk to Boromir\tIt would seem Boromir's own journey came to a successful end, and the soldier of Gondor is pleased to see you.\n9\tWalk with Boromir and tell him what transpired after you parted\tBoromir wants to know what transpired after the three of you parted ways.\n10\tTalk to Boromir by the Last Homely House\tYou told Boromir some of what befell you and Meneldir after the three of you parted, and the soldier of Gondor has spent much of the walk in silence.\n11\tTalk to Gandalf the Grey outside the Last Homely House\tGandalf the Grey has greeted you outside the Last Homely House, desiring to speak with you.\n12\tTalk to Elrond outside the Last Homely House\tElrond, the master of the house, desires to hear your story.\n",
[6968]="7002EE3E\n1\tTalk to Ingmar\tSpeak with Lord Ingmar.\n2\tFight through the mounted defences of Maustazg\tFight your way through the mounted defences of Maustazg.\n3\tTalk to Ingmar\tSpeak with Lord Ingmar.\n4\tFight your way to the centre of Maustazg\tFight your way to the centre of Maustazg.\n5\tConfront Hoital\tConfront Hoital, leader of the Orcs at Maustazg.\n6\tListen to the conversation\tListen to what Hoital has to say.\n7\tDefeat Hoital and his minions\tDefeat Hoital.\n8\tTalk to Ingmar\tIngmar lies wounded in the central camp of Maustazg. You should speak with Ingmar and leave Maustazg behind.\n",
[6969]="7003A2B2\n1\tSpeak with Éowyn\tÉowyn is in Edoras. You should speak with Éowyn.\n2\tFollow Éowyn\tÉowyn is in Edoras. You should follow Éowyn.\n3\tRouse Éowyn from her unhappy reverie\tÉowyn is in Edoras. You should speak with Éowyn.\n4\tListen to Éowyn\tÉowyn is in Edoras. You should listen to Éowyn.\n5\tListen to Éowyn\tÉowyn is in Edoras. You should speak with Éowyn.\n6\tJoin Éowyn in battle\tÉowyn is ready to face the foe that threatens Edoras.\n7\tFight alongside Éowyn\tFight alongside Éowyn.\n8\tSpeak with Éowyn\tSpeak with Éowyn.\n",
[6970]="7006AA22\n1\tTalk to Mêshka\tMêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is almost ready to begin. You should talk to Mêshka.\n2\tAdmire the mural\tMêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is ready to begin. You should take a moment to look at the mural.\n3\tAttend the memorial\tMêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is beginning.\n4\tTalk to Belondor\tMêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. The families of the deceased mariners have tried to absolve Belondor of his feelings of guilt. Belondor wants to talk to you.\n",
[6971]="70064BEB\n1\tTalk to Rossaran in the Palace of the Swan\tThe Swan-knight Rossaran has brought you before the Prince of Dol Amroth, as King Elessar desired.\n2\tWait for your audience with the Prince of Dol Amroth\tKing Elessar and Queen Arwen wait to discuss important matters with Imrahil, Prince of Dol Amroth.\n3\tTalk to Queen Arwen in the Palace of the Swan\tQueen Arwen has asked to speak with you.\n4\tSet the bowl of water down on the floor where Queen Arwen indicated\tQueen Arwen has indicated a place on the floor where she wants you to set down the bowl of water.\n5\tWait for Queen Arwen to explain herself\tWait until Queen Arwen explains her peculiar words and deeds.\n6\tTalk to Roamingstar in the Palace of the Swan\tRoamingstar has appeared in the Palace of the Swan.\n7\tTalk to Dorthaneth in the Palace of the Swan\tDorthaneth stands in the Palace of the Swan.\n8\tListen to the words of Dorthaneth\tDorthaneth stands in the Palace of the Swan.\n9\tTalk to King Elessar in the Palace of the Swan\tKing Elessar waits patiently for his audience with Prince Imrahil to begin.\n",
[6972]="70027B08\n1\tTalk to Fâsh inside Orthanc\tFâsh has brought you inside Orthanc and is waiting to speak with you.\n2\tYou have been summoned inside Orthanc to present yourself to Saruman and have been ordered not to stray from the path.\t\n3\tTalk to Saruman in the tower of Orthanc\tSaruman has brought you to a library within his tower of Orthanc.\n4\tResist the power of Saruman's voice (use /resist)\tThe power of Saruman's voice is seductive, his words convincing. You find yourself nodding in agreement. You must resist. You must not succumb.\n5\tTalk to Saruman in the tower of Orthanc\tThe power of Saruman's voice is seductive, his words convincing. You find yourself nodding in agreement. You must resist. You must not succumb.\n6\tResist the power of Saruman's voice (use /resist)\tThe power of Saruman's voice is seductive, his words convincing. You find yourself nodding in agreement. You must resist. You must not succumb.\n7\tListen to Saruman within Orthanc\tThe power of Saruman's voice is seductive, his words convincing. You find yourself nodding in agreement. You must resist. You must not succumb.\n8\tResist the power of Saruman's voice (use /resist)\tThe power of Saruman's voice is seductive, his words convincing. You find yourself nodding in agreement. You must resist. You must not succumb.\n9\tListen to Saruman within Orthanc\tThe power of Saruman's voice is seductive, his words convincing. You find yourself nodding in agreement. You must resist. You must not succumb.\n10\tTalk to Gun Ain\tYou have not seen the Angmarim once known as Avair since you were in Forochel. Her name was taken from her, and now she serves Saruman as Gun Ain, 'Without Name.'\n11\tListen to Saruman within Orthanc\tYou have not seen the Angmarim once known as Avair since you were in Forochel. Her name was taken from her, and now she serves Saruman as Gun Ain, 'Without Name.'\n",
[6973]="70049A86\n1\tTalk to Harthalín\tYou should speak to Harthalín. You and your companion, Harthalín, have marched in the Last Alliance for years under the command of High King Gil-galad.\n2\tAttend the High King's address to the Alliance\tHigh King Gil-galad and the commanders of the Alliance are standing at the head of the rear garrison. Harthalín has asked you to join her at the High King's address to the Alliance on the eve of a great battle.\n3\tListen to High King Gil-galad and Elendil the Tall\tHigh King Gil-galad and Elendil the Tall are speaking to the Alliance.\n4\tConfront the Gwetherain\tYou should stand with the High King and the other commanders of the Alliance. The Gwetherain are approaching the rear garrison of the Alliance.\n5\tTalk to High King Gil-galad\tHigh King Gil-galad is standing outside the rear garrison upon the Dagorlad. You have stood fast before the Gwetherain, and the High King now wishes to speak with you.\n6\tLearn the fates of the Spears of Lindon and their garrison\tThe forward garrison lies across the flaming trenches of the Enemy to the south of the rear garrison. The High King has asked you to scout the forward garrison and relay a message to his kindred: the Spears of Lindon.\n7\tDernaith and Megoril can be found at the forward garrison upon the Dagorlad. You have found two of the Spears of Lindon, but you have not found Thelaron. You should speak to Dernaith and Megoril.\t\n8\tRescue wounded soldiers from the Orcs west of the forward garrison ([see journal]/5)\tWounded soldiers can be found to the west of the forward garrison upon the Dagorlad. Dernaith and Megoril have alerted you to the recent passing of one of the Gwetherain, the Cursed Rider, which scattered their forces and left many wounded upon the battle plain.\n9\tRescue Prince Thranduil to the west of the forward garrison\tPrince Thranduil can be found far to the west of the forward garrison in a webbed vale. One of the Gwetherain, the Cursed Rider, has driven Prince Thranduil into a nearby vale where he is now trapped. You should aid Thranduil in repelling the Cursed Rider.\n10\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond can be found in the webbed vale to the west of the forward garrison. You, Elrond, and Glorfindel have repelled the terrible spawn of Ungwetári that threatened the Cursed Rider and Thranduil alike. You should now speak to Elrond.\n11\tReunite with the Alliance at the forward garrison\tThe Alliance has come to the forward garrison upon the Dagorlad. Elrond Halfelven has brought word of the Alliance's advance, and High King Gil-galad has requested your presence at the forward garrison.\n12\tTalk to High King Gil-galad at the forward garrison\tHigh King Gil-galad can be found at the forward garrison upon the Dagorlad. You have arrived to find the Alliance gathered at the forward garrison. You should now speak to High King Gil-galad as he requested.\n13\tTalk to Slégar the Crafty\tSlégar the Crafty can be found at the forward garrison upon the Dagorlad. High King Gil-galad has sent you upon a two-fold mission: to provide a distraction for the Alliance and to rescue the Spear of Lindon, Thelaron. Before setting out, you should speak to Slégar the Crafty of Durin's Folk.\n14\tSet the Enemy's barrels of black powder aflame (total: 6)\tBarrels of black powder can be found to the east of the forward garrison upon the Dagorlad. Slégar the Crafty has asked you to find what remains of the Enemy's black powder and set it aflame. He hopes that it will provide a distraction for the Alliance to advance upon the Black Gate.\n15\tFind and follow the Gwatharan's path\tYou should seek any sign of the Gwatharan's passing and follow his path. You have provided the distraction needed by the Alliance. You should now seek Thelaron and follow the path of the Gwatharan that took him.\n16\tTalk to Harthalín\tHarthalín can be found with her company beyond the eastern trenches upon the Dagorlad. You have discovered Harthalín and her company while searching for Thelaron. You should speak to her and see if any among her company might aid you.\n17\tLearn of Thelaron's fate from Prince Amroth\tPrince Amroth is among Harthalín's company. You have arrived to find Harthalín and her company tending the wounds of Prince Amroth. Amroth claims to have seen one of the Gwetherain pass with an Elf on his steed.\n18\tTalk to Harthalín\tHarthalín can be found with her company beyond the eastern trenches upon the Dagorlad. You have learned that the Witch-king himself took Thelaron, and should now speak to Harthalín and plan a rescue.\n19\tSearch the encampment for any sign of Thelaron or the Witch-king\tThe Easterling encampment lies far to the east of the forward garrison. Harthalín has led you to the far end of the Easterling encampment, and you should now search for any sign of Thelaron or the Witch-king.\n20\tConfront the Witch-king and rescue Thelaron\tThe Witch-king can be found atop the overlook beyond the Easterling encampment. You have tracked the Witch-king's steed to the far end of the Easterling encampment and should now climb the long stairs to the overlook. You must confront the Witch-king and rescue Thelaron.\n21\tMumble at Harthalín and try to move (Select Harthalín and type '/mumble')\tHarthalín can be found at your bedside in Tham Send in the Last Homely House. You have awoken from your encounter with the Witch-king within the haven of Imladris. Harthalín now sits at your bedside. You should try to speak to her. NOTE: Select Harthalín and type '/mumble' to advance the quest.\n22\tRest until your wound is healed\tYou have endured great suffering as a result of the wound dealt to you by the Witch-king. You should continue resting until you are fully healed.\n23\tFind Elrond in the Last Homely House\tElrond Halfelven can be found somewhere within Tham Send in the Last Homely House. You have awoken from your long slumber and should now seek Elrond.\n24\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond Halfelven can be found within Tham Send in the Last Homely House. You have found Elrond, and you should now speak with him.\n25\tWalk with Elrond\tElrond Halfelven can be found within Tham Send in the Last Homely House. Elrond is speaking to you of the great battle against Sauron and the fates of your kindred.\n26\tLearn of Hithgol's condition in Tham Send\tHithgol can be found in one of the beds in Tham Send in the Last Homely House. Hithgol, the warrior and herbalist who once aided Prince Amroth, sustained a blow from the Dark Lord. You should learn of his condition, and see if he shall soon be healed as well.\n27\tTalk to Elrond, gather your belongings, and depart on your journey with his sons\tElrond has given you leave to travel to Celondim in preparation to sail to the havens of Mithlond, but you shall have need of supplies for your journey.\n",
[6974]="7006826C\n1\tPick up the bowl of sea-water on the bridge to the Citadel of Winds\tYou should pick up the bowl of sea-water and carry it across the bridge to the island, bringing it past the defences and up the hill into the Citadel of Winds. Do not drop the bowl or spill any of the water! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Water-bearer Ushu south-east of the fountain\tThe other water-bearers stand to the south-east of the fountain inside the Citadel of Winds.\n3\tEavesdrop upon the conversation of the Kindred of the Coins inside the Citadel of Winds\tSeveral members of the Kindred of the Coins guard their captive inside the Citadel of Winds.\n4\tEavesdrop upon the confrontation of the Kindred of the Coins with Jajax and his captive\tSeveral members of the Kindred of the Coins meet with Jajax inside the Citadel of Winds.\n5\tTalk to Azagath Sea-shadow in the Citadel of Winds\tAzagath has noticed you within the Citadel of Winds.\n6\tSurvive the attention of the Kindred of the Coins in the Citadel of Winds\tThe Kindred of the Coins has obtained a new, more valuable hostage: you!\n7\tWitness the confrontation\tThe bubbling fountain in the Citadel of Winds heralds the arrival of an unexpected presence.\n8\tTalk to Jajax's captive\tJajax's captive is in the Citadel of Winds.\n9\tTalk to Jajax in the Citadel of Winds\tJajax is in the Citadel of Winds.\n",
[6975]="7004A909\n1\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli can be found on the precipice within the abyss of Mordath. You descended into the abyss of Mordath and have come to a ledge within depths of Barad-dûr. You should speak to Gimli and begin your search for King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns.\n2\tSearch the depths of Barad-dûr for King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns\tGimli can be found in the depths of Barad-dûr. You are searching the depths of Barad-dûr for King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns. You should follow Gimli and keep a keen eye on the shadowed tunnels of the Dark Tower.\n3\tTalk to Gimli in the Chamber of the Watchers\tGimli is standing in the Chamber of the Watchers in the depths of Barad-dûr. You and Gimli have found a grisly trail of slain followers of the Order of the Eye leading to the Chamber of the Watchers. A statue of Sauron looms ahead and its gaze is fixed upon you. You should speak to Gimli.\n4\tConfront the glamour in the Chamber of the Watchers\tThe glamour can be found in the Chamber of the Watchers in Barad-dûr. A glamour has risen from the statue of Sauron in the Chamber of the Watchers. You and Gimli must stand fast!\n5\tTalk to Gimli in the Chamber of the Watchers\tGimli can be found in the Chamber of the Watchers in Barad-dûr. You have repelled the attacks of a glamour, one of the remnants of the Dark Lord himself, which warned of an insidious trap laid for the Firehorns and King Váskmun Greytooth. You should now speak to Gimli.\n",
[6976]="700544AB\n1\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n2\tSecure the tower\tSecure the tower. It is recommended to have the quest The Circle of Madness underway.\n3\tTalk to one of the Rangers\tTalk to one of the Rangers.\n",
})
